UPDATE companies SET description='Universal Solar, LLC is a solar installation and service company based in Millersburg, Pennsylvania. The company has been operating for nearly a decade, focusing on energy-efficient solutions for rural areas prone to blackouts. The business is operated by Elmer, who is frequently cited in customer reviews for his hands-on expertise and responsiveness.

The company designs and installs off-grid, grid-tied, and grid-interactive solar systems for residential, commercial, and industrial clients. Its service portfolio includes solar panel installation and repair, battery storage solutions, system maintenance and inspection, and well pump installations. Universal Solar serves a multi-county region in central and northeastern Pennsylvania, including Millersburg, Bloomsburg, Lewisburg, Williamsport, and Scranton.

Customers range from homeowners seeking backup power to businesses and industrial facilities aiming to lower energy costs. Commercial projects include roof-mounted arrays for businesses, while industrial installations target facility-scale energy production.

Universal Solar was motivated by the vulnerability of the electrical grid and aims to help customers achieve energy independence. The company offers free estimates and financing options to reduce upfront costs.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Off-grid solar system installation", "Grid-tied solar system installation", "Grid-interactive solar system installation", "Solar panel installation", "Solar panel repair", "Battery storage installation", "Solar system maintenance and inspection", "Well pump installation", "Commercial solar installation", "Industrial solar installation", "Roof-mounted solar panel installation"], "industries": ["Residential", "Commercial", "Industrial"], "materials": [], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Free estimates for solar projects", "Financing options available", "Nearly a decade of solar installation experience", "Focus on energy independence and grid resilience", "Service across central and northeastern Pennsylvania"], "facts_used": ["Location: Millersburg, PA -> /", "Services: off-grid, grid-tied, grid-interactive, solar panel installation/repair, battery storage, maintenance, well pump -> /", "Industries served: residential, commercial, industrial -> /", "Experience: nearly a decade -> /", "Financing options and free estimates -> /", "Service area: multiple PA counties -> /", "Lead technician Elmer mentioned in reviews -> /", "Company name, slug, description, headquarters -> db"], "company_type": "Installer / service company", "makes_products": "no", "type_evidence": "Our services include: Off solar grid system, Grid-tied solar system, Interactive grid, Solar panel installation, Well pump", "founded_year": "", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='universal-solar-llc' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Uptown Millworks operates from the Uptown neighborhood of New Orleans, Louisiana, as a locally owned and operated custom millwork shop. The company was founded by Christian Pokorn, who comes from a multi‑generational woodworking family in Austria and spent summers in his family’s sawmill. After building a career in construction as the principal of Pokorn Construction, Pokorn established Uptown Millworks to focus on custom architectural millwork and historically faithful restoration for New Orleans homes.

The shop produces a full range of millwork and furniture, including handrails, flooring, cypress slabs, custom cabinets, moldings, windows, doors, shutters, and turnings. Using time‑tested woodworking techniques alongside modern precision tools, the team of millwrights, carpenters, and woodworkers fabricates every piece in their New Orleans workshop.

Uptown Millworks serves residential, hospitality, and commercial clients across Louisiana, with projects in private homes, restaurants, hotels, and historic buildings. The company coordinates directly with customers and vendors on architectural millwork, casework, and restoration work that meets the standards of the Architectural Woodwork Institute, the Forest Stewardship Council, and the NOLA Historic District Landmarks Commission.

Pokorn emphasizes building with honor and integrity, describing quality as the company’s entire philosophy. The operation prioritizes local manufacturing to create jobs, sources FSC‑certified and sustainable woods, and delivers finished pieces with its own crew to keep the carbon footprint low. Offcuts and sawdust are repurposed in the shop or donated to community gardens and animal shelters, reflecting a commitment to resource stewardship.', certifications=ARRAY['Architectural Woodwork Institute (AWI) standards','Forest Stewardship Council (FSC) standards','NOLA Historic District Landmarks Commission regulations']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Handrails", "Flooring", "Cypress slabs", "Custom projects", "Moldings and millwork", "Windows, doors and shutters", "Custom cabinets", "Turnings", "Architectural millwork", "Casework", "Custom furniture", "Historically faithful restoration", "Precision woodworking", "Sustainable material sourcing", "FSC\u2011certified material procurement", "Low\u2011carbon delivery", "In\u2011house installation", "Waste recycling and repurposing"], "industries": ["Residential", "Hospitality", "Commercial", "Historic restoration", "Architectural millwork"], "materials": ["Cypress", "FSC\u2011certified wood", "Sustainable local woods", "Natural wood"], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["All millwork and furniture sourced, manufactured, and finished in New Orleans", "Work adheres to AWI, FSC, and NOLA Historic District Landmarks Commission standards", "Materials purchased per project with no standing inventory", "Waste cutoffs, scraps, and sawdust repurposed or donated", "In\u2011house delivery and installation by the company\u2019s own team"], "facts_used": ["Founded in Uptown New Orleans, Louisiana -> /about-us", "Founder Christian Pokorn from Austria, family sawmill -> /about-us", "Locally owned and operated custom millwork shop -> /about-us", "Services: Handrails, Flooring, Cypress Slabs, Custom projects, Moldings and millwork, Windows, doors and shutters, Custom cabinets, Turnings -> /services", "Adherence to AWI, FSC, NOLA Historic District Landmarks Commission standards -> /quality", "All work sourced, manufactured, finished in New Orleans -> /", "No inventory, materials purchased per job -> /quality", "Waste repurposed or donated -> /quality", "Delivery and installation by own team -> /quality", "Serve Louisiana houses, restaurants, hotels, commercial spaces -> /", "Team of millwrights, carpenters, woodworkers with over ten years experience -> /about-us", "Use time-tested woodworking techniques and precision tools -> /about-us", "Focus on sustainable woods, low carbon footprint -> /quality", "Historically faithful restoration -> /about-us"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "Uptown Millworks is a New Orleans millwork shop and furniture maker specializing in quality, style and function.", "founded_year": "", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='uptown-millworks' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Urth Apparel Inc. is a custom apparel manufacturer based in Newport Beach, California. Founded in 2013, the company began as an international trade cooperative focused on natural foods and cotton apparel from Peru. The founder started the venture after struggling to find a factory that shared a passion for fashionable products beyond basic tees and cared for the environment and workers.

The company provides end-to-end product development and manufacturing services, including fashion and technical design, fabric and trim sourcing, pattern making, grading, marker making, sampling, cutting and sewing, screen printing, sublimation, heat transfer, finishing, packaging, and inspection. Production is split across three origins: luxury clothing in Italy, knitwear and basics in Peru, and specialty technical apparel in the USA. Urth Apparel runs dedicated production lines for tees, tanks, and polos, and emphasizes sustainable and organic materials. The team consists of three employees at the Newport Beach headquarters, coordinating with overseas factories.

Urth Apparel serves clothing brands of all sizes, from startups to established labels, across categories such as tees and tanks, dresses, kids and baby apparel, yoga and athleisure wear, swimwear, and dress shirts. The company works with brands seeking a one-stop partner for concept-to-market apparel production, offering daily communication between design teams in the USA and Europe and production floors abroad.

The founders created Urth Apparel because they were unhappy with existing manufacturing partners that delivered non-uniform quality, poor business practices, and high minimums. Their philosophy centers on doing it right: taking care of the planet, taking care of workers, and creating clothing that lasts. The company positions itself as an ethical clothing factory that makes sustainable manufacturing easy for brands.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Product Development", "Pattern Making", "Marker Making", "Cutting & Sewing", "Screen Printing", "Textile Sublimation", "Heat Transfer", "Heat Bonding", "Sampling & Prototyping", "Technical Design", "Quality Control", "Fabric Sourcing", "Trim Sourcing", "Grading", "Finishing", "Packaging", "Inspection", "Embroidery", "Chenille", "Digital Printing"], "industries": ["Apparel", "Fashion", "Sportswear", "Children''s apparel", "Swimwear"], "materials": ["Organic cotton", "Modal", "Sustainable fabrics"], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Production split by origin: luxury in Italy, knitwear/basics in Peru, technical apparel in USA", "Dedicated production lines for tees, tanks, and polos", "Emphasis on sustainable and organic materials", "One-stop shop from concept through production", "Daily communication between design teams and production floor"], "facts_used": ["Founded in 2013 as an international trade cooperative -> /about-us", "Headquartered in Newport Beach, California -> db", "Three employees -> db", "Production split across Italy, Peru, USA -> /", "Services include product development, pattern making, cutting and sewing, screen printing, sublimation, heat transfer -> /", "Dedicated production lines for tees, tanks, polos -> /", "Emphasis on sustainable and organic materials -> /", "Serves clothing brands across categories: tees, dresses, kids, yoga, swimwear, dress shirts -> /", "Founders motivated by dissatisfaction with existing manufacturers'' quality, practices, minimums -> /about-us", "Philosophy: take care of planet, workers, create lasting clothing -> /about-us", "Three-step model: email, talk to expert, samples & manufacturing -> /", "Free consultation offered -> /", "Team includes Head of Growth Alexander J. Soler -> /about-us", "No explicit ownership tags -> db", "No certifications mentioned -> db", "No equipment named -> db", "No volume, lead time, tolerances stated -> db", "No cage code, min order, export compliance, languages, social links -> db"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "Urth Apparel Inc. is a custom apparel manufacturer based in Newport Beach, California, that takes clothing brands from concept through production.", "founded_year": "2013", "employee_count": "3", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='urth-apparel-inc' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Utah Breakers & Supply was established in May 2003 in Salt Lake City, Utah, starting in a 6,000-square-foot building. The company has since relocated to a 12,000-square-foot warehouse to accommodate growing inventory levels.

The firm buys and sells new, used, obsolete, and hard-to-find electrical equipment, with a focus on circuit breakers, hardware kits, transformers, safety switches, bus plugs, MCC buckets, and starters. It operates a reconditioning and refurbishing program that adheres to manufacturer specifications, using load-testing equipment to verify performance. All refurbished products carry a one-year warranty.

Utah Breakers emphasizes same-day shipping on stocked items, a one-year warranty on all products, and a strict reconditioning process designed to meet original manufacturer standards.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Electrical equipment reconditioning", "Load testing", "Circuit breaker refurbishment", "Obsolete electrical parts sourcing", "Warranty service", "Same-day shipping"], "industries": [], "materials": [], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "Same-day shipping for stocked items", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Same-day shipping on stocked parts", "One-year warranty on all products", "Load-tested reconditioned equipment", "Strict reconditioning standards meeting manufacturer specifications", "12,000-square-foot inventory warehouse"], "facts_used": ["Founded May 2003 in Salt Lake City, Utah -> /", "Relocated from 6,000 to 12,000 sq ft warehouse -> /", "Buys and sells new, used, obsolete electrical equipment -> /", "Specializes in circuit breakers, hardware kits, transformers, safety switches, bus plugs, MCC buckets, starters -> /", "Reconditioning and refurbishing to manufacturer specifications -> /", "Load-testing and one-year warranty on all products -> /", "Same-day shipping advertised -> /", "Headquarters Salt Lake City, Utah -> db", "Founded 2003 -> db"], "company_type": "Distributor / reseller", "makes_products": "no", "type_evidence": "Utah Breakers buys and sells new, used, obsolete, and hard-to-find electrical equipment specializing in circuit breakers, hardware kits, transformers, safety switches, bus plugs, MCC buckets, and starters.", "founded_year": "2003", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='utah-breakers-supply' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='The shop builds several distinct collections: Aspen, crafted from eco-friendly dead-standing aspen logs; Barnwood, made from reclaimed barn wood, chicken coops, and snow fencing; Rocky Mountain, using smaller rustic logs with optional wildlife carvings and twig handles; Slimline, a space-saving series; and Salt River Rustic, a newer in-house line. A custom program allows clients to specify dimensions, stains, tiles, and carvings. Pieces are handcrafted on-site, and the company highlights a lacquer finish on its solid-wood bathroom furniture.

The furniture targets residential customers furnishing homes and cabins, as well as commercial spaces such as lodges or hospitality venues. Sales are direct to the end user through the company''s website.

