UPDATE companies SET description='Utility Wire Products, Inc. operates from a 48,000-square-foot facility on Cleveland''s industrial East Side, at 3302 East 87th Street. The company was founded in 1953 by Ed Peck and Bill Milavac. Donald Anzells purchased the business in 1980 and has led it as a family-owned, trans-generational operation; his son Ronald Anzells serves as president after 30 years with the firm, and Ronald Anzells Jr. joined in 2007 as plant manager and custom tooling specialist.

The shop specializes in custom wire forming across five major product lines: point-of-purchase display racks, wire guards for lighting, fans, machinery and heaters, wire baskets, wire forms, and grids. It works wire diameters from .080 to .500 inch in bright basic, stainless steel, and galvanized wire, and incorporates tubing, sheet metal, and plastics. An on-site 3D CNC bending machine supports both prototyping and production runs of 1 to 500,000 units. Finishing options include powder coating, vinyl, nylon, and various platings.

Customers span retail chains needing plan-o-gram display systems, industrial OEMs requiring protective guards, medical facilities using baskets for hospital stretchers, and manufacturers sourcing wire forms for screw-machine parts. The company accepts orders as small as a single unit and scales to high-volume production.

The firm''s stated philosophy is to deliver a "Quality Product in a Timely Fashion at a Fair Price that are American made," treating every order — whether one piece or half a million — with equal importance and personal attention.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Custom wire forming", "3D CNC wire bending", "Point-of-purchase display manufacturing", "Wire guard fabrication", "Wire basket fabrication", "Wire grid manufacturing", "Powder coating", "Vinyl coating", "Nylon coating", "Plating", "Design assistance", "Prototyping", "Low-volume production", "High-volume production"], "industries": ["Consumer products", "Retail", "Industrial", "Medical", "Manufacturing"], "materials": ["Bright basic wire", "Stainless steel wire", "Galvanized wire", "Tubing", "Sheet metal", "Plastics"], "equipment": ["3D CNC Bending Machine"], "volume": "1 to 500,000 units", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Orders accepted from a single unit to 500,000 pieces", "Family-owned since 1980 with second-generation leadership", "On-site 3D CNC wire bending machine", "48,000 sq ft facility combining production and warehousing", "All products made in the USA"], "facts_used": ["Founded 1953 by Ed Peck and Bill Milavac -> /about", "Donald Anzells purchased company in 1980 -> /about", "Family-owned, trans-generational -> /about", "Ronald Anzells president (30 years), Ronald Anzells Jr. plant manager since 2007 -> /about", "48,000 sq ft facility in Cleveland -> /, /about", "Five major product lines, wire diameters .080 to .500 -> /about", "On-site 3D CNC Bending Machine -> /about", "Materials: bright basic, stainless steel, galvanized wire, tubing, sheet metal, plastics -> /about", "Coatings: powder coating, vinyl, nylon, plating -> /about", "Volume range 1 to 500,000 units -> /about", "Minimum order 1 unit -> /, /about", "Motto: Quality Product in a Timely Fashion at a Fair Price, American made -> /about", "Industries implied: retail (POP displays), industrial (guards), medical (hospital baskets), manufacturing (screw machine parts) -> /, /about", "Headquarters: 3302 East 87th St, Cleveland, Ohio 44127 -> /, /about"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "Utility Wire Products, Inc. is a custom wire product manufacturer.", "founded_year": "1953", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "1 unit", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": ["Family-owned"]}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='utility-wire-products' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='V-Tron Electronics Corporation, based in Attleboro, Massachusetts, was incorporated in 1970 as a privately held, veteran-owned small business. The company began as an electronics service provider to the emerging Massachusetts computer industry in the 1970s before expanding into semiconductors, medical, military, and industrial electronics. President Doug Gobin emphasizes that quality and reliability are keys to survival in a competitive market.

The company manufactures custom cable assemblies, wire harnesses, fiber optic assemblies, molded connector assemblies, and box build integrations in a 45,000-square-foot facility. Processes include low- and high-pressure molding with PVC, polyurethane, polypropylene, TPE, and TPA; fiber optic termination; and full box build with sheet metal chassis. V-Tron handles low to high volume order lot sizes, using a real-time bar-coded ERP system to track jobs from order inception through final inspection. Every assembly undergoes 100% functional testing, with Cirris 4250 scanners automating electrical tests on cables and harnesses.

V-Tron serves defense and security, military, life sciences, medical, semiconductor, and industrial electronics customers. Its assemblies are built to IPC standards in an ISO 9001:2015 environment, with UL and cUL recognition (E76510, E173242) and CSA certification (LR56498-1). The in-house training program, led by an IPC-certified instructor, ensures associates meet J-STD-001, IPC-A-610, and IPC/WHMA-A-620 workmanship requirements.

Founded on the principle that quality cannot be inspected into a product, V-Tron differentiates itself through reverse engineering and pre-production manufacturability analysis, a functional guarantee on every harness, and a culture of continuous improvement driven by its quality management system.', certifications=ARRAY['ISO 9001:2015','UL recognized wiring harness program (E76510)','UL listed power supply cord program (E173242)','CSA certified (LR56498-1)']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Custom cable assembly", "Wire harness assembly", "Fiber optic assembly", "Molded connector assembly (low- and high-pressure molding)", "Box build assembly", "Process engineering and pre-production manufacturability analysis", "ERP/MRP system for real-time job tracking", "Bar-coded job travelers", "100% functional testing (Cirris 4250 scanners)", "Fiber optic testing (dB loss, visual inspection)", "Crimp integrity tensile testing", "Custom test fixture development", "In-house IPC training (J-STD-001, IPC-A-610, IPC/WHMA-A-620)", "Reverse engineering and documentation", "Consigned, KANBAN, and bonded inventory systems"], "industries": ["Defense and Security", "Military", "Life Sciences", "Medical", "Semiconductors", "Industrial Electronics"], "materials": ["Polyvinyl Chloride (PVC)", "Polyurethane (PUR)", "Polypropylene (PP)", "Thermoplastic Elastomers (TPE)", "Thermoplastic Polyamides (TPA)", "Optical glass (fiber optic)"], "equipment": ["Cirris 4250 scanners", "Tensile testing equipment", "Custom fabricated electrical harness boards", "Light meters for fiber optic inspection", "Computer-aided software for fiber optic inspection"], "volume": "Low to high volume order lot sizes", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["100% functional testing on every assembly with automated Cirris 4250 scanners", "Real-time bar-coded ERP system tracking orders from receipt to shipment", "In-house IPC-certified training program (J-STD-001, IPC-A-610, IPC/WHMA-A-620)", "Reverse engineering and pre-production manufacturability analysis for each new part", "Veteran-owned small business with ISO 9001:2015, UL, and CSA certifications"], "facts_used": ["Founded 1970, veteran-owned small business, incorporated in Massachusetts -> /about-us", "45,000sf facility, low to high volume production -> /about-us", "Services: cable assemblies, wire harnesses, fiber optic assemblies, molded connectors, box build -> /services", "Industries: defense/military, life sciences/medical, semiconductors, industrial electronics -> /about-us", "Certifications: ISO 9001:2015, UL E76510, UL E173242, CSA LR56498-1 -> /about-us, /quality", "Equipment: Cirris 4250 scanners, tensile testing equipment, custom harness boards, light meters -> /quality", "Materials: PVC, PUR, PP, TPE, TPA for molded connectors -> /services", "Processes: reverse engineering, ERP system, bar-coded travelers, IPC training -> /about-us, /capabilities, /quality", "President Doug Gobin message and mission statement -> /", "Functional guarantee on every harness -> /capabilities", "100% testing on all products -> /quality"], "company_type": "Contract manufacturer / job shop", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "We effectively produce low to high volume order lot sizes in our 45,000sf Massachusetts facility to our customers\u2019 exact specifications.", "founded_year": "1970", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": ["Veteran-owned", "Small business"]}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='v-tron-electronics-corporation' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Vip Rubber and Plastic operates from Minden, Nevada, where it has been manufacturing rubber and plastic products since 1961. The company was founded by Howard Vipperman Sr., known as “Big Vip,” who entered the rubber industry as a gasket cutter after serving in the armed forces. It remains a family-owned business led by subsequent generations.

The facility produces custom and standard rubber extrusions, rubber sheet and rolls, molded rubber parts, and custom rubber compounds. On the plastic side, it runs plastic extrusion lines for profiles, pipe, tubing, vinyl spline, and window and door seals. A merger with Excalibur Extrusions expanded its plastic extrusion capacity. The company also offers value-added fabrication under its Vip+ Services banner, positioning itself as a one-stop shop.

Its customer base spans agriculture, aerospace, automotive, architectural glass and metal, and construction. The aerospace segment includes approvals to several Boeing material specifications, and the quality system holds AS9100 certification. The company notes it has produced parts for virtually every industry over its history.

Vip Rubber and Plastic emphasizes honesty and integrity as core values, and highlights its domestic manufacturing—all products are made in the USA. The founder’s hands-on experience on the shop floor is cited as the foundation for the company’s technical depth and long-term customer relationships.', certifications=ARRAY['AS9100','ISO9001','ITAR','ROHS']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Rubber extrusion (profiles, solid rod, cord)", "Rubber sheet and roll manufacturing", "Molded rubber parts", "Custom rubber compounding", "Value-added fabrication (Vip+ Services)", "Plastic extrusion (profiles, pipe, tubing)", "Plastic pipe extrusion", "Vinyl spline extrusion", "Extruded window and door seals", "Custom plastic fabrication", "Precision rubber products"], "industries": ["Agriculture", "Aerospace", "Automotive", "Architectural Glass & Metal", "Construction", "Custom"], "materials": ["Rubber compounds", "Plastic resins", "Custom compounds", "Spec materials"], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Family-owned and operated since 1961", "AS9100 certified and approved for Boeing material specifications", "In-house custom rubber compounding", "Value-added fabrication (Vip+ Services) for one-stop shopping", "All products manufactured in the USA"], "facts_used": ["Founded 1961 by Howard Vipperman Sr. -> /", "Family-owned -> /", "Headquarters in Minden, Nevada -> db", "Certifications: AS9100, ISO9001, ITAR, ROHS -> db", "Approved for Boeing material specifications -> /", "Industries served: Agriculture, Aerospace, Automotive, Architectural Glass & Metal, Construction, Custom -> /", "Capabilities: rubber extrusion, rubber sheet, molded rubber, custom compounding, plastic extrusion, plastic pipe, vinyl spline, window/door seals, value-added fabrication -> /", "Merger with Excalibur Extrusions -> /", "All products manufactured in USA -> /", "Core values: honesty & integrity -> /"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "We are a family owned American manufacturer of rubber and plastic products, founded in 1961, by Howard Vipperman Sr.", "founded_year": "1961", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": ["ITAR registered"], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": ["Family-owned"]}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='vip-plastics-and-rubber-manufacturing' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Vermont Manufacturing Services (VMS) operates from West Rutland, Vermont, where it has provided contract manufacturing, fulfillment, and packaging services for more than 30 years. The company was acquired in 2011 by Jessica Dambrackas, who purchased the business from its previous incarnation as Rutland Industries.

The company runs a 12,000-square-foot facility with climate-controlled warehousing and loading docks. Its services span kitting, packaging, and assembly (including hand assembly), pick-and-pack order fulfillment, e-commerce integration, warehousing, cross-docking, quality control, distribution, and inventory management.

VMS serves electronic manufacturers, food packaging companies, e-commerce retailers, fashion labels, and publishing houses such as the Rutland Herald.

Dambrackas established a mission to employ as many individuals with disabilities as possible, and the company operates on lean manufacturing principles. VMS also emphasizes fixed pricing to simplify forecasting and offers e-commerce software that connects to shopping carts within minutes.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Quality Control", "Distribution", "Inventory Management", "Kitting", "Packaging", "Assembly", "Pick & Pack", "E-commerce Fulfillment", "Warehousing", "Cross-Docking", "Hand Assembly"], "industries": ["Electronics manufacturing", "Food packaging", "E-commerce", "Fashion", "Publishing"], "materials": [], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["12,000 sq ft facility with climate-controlled warehousing", "Over 30 years of contract manufacturing and fulfillment experience", "E-commerce software integrates with shopping carts in minutes", "Fixed pricing simplifies expense forecasting", "Mission-driven employment for individuals with disabilities"], "facts_used": ["Location: West Rutland, Vermont -> db", "Acquired by Jessica Dambrackas in 2011 -> /about", "Formerly Rutland Industries -> /about", "Over 30 years experience -> /", "12,000 sq ft facility -> /", "Climate-controlled warehousing -> /", "Services: kitting, packaging, assembly, pick & pack, e-commerce fulfillment, warehousing, cross-docking, quality control, distribution, inventory management -> /", "Industries served: electronic manufacturers, food packaging, ecommerce, fashion, publishing -> /", "Rutland Herald as client -> /", "Mission to employ individuals with disabilities -> /about", "Lean manufacturing principles -> /", "Fixed pricing -> /", "E-commerce software connects in minutes -> /", "Loading docks and overhead doors -> /", "Respond to inquiries within 24-48 hours -> /"], "company_type": "Contract manufacturer / job shop", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "contract manufacturing, fulfillment, and packaging company", "founded_year": "", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='vms-fulfillment-assembly-and-warehousing' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Valley Woodcraft & Lumber Co., based in Wilkes-Barre, Pennsylvania, was founded in 1952. The company operates as a small, veteran-owned contract manufacturer serving a range of industrial sectors.

The shop produces custom wood, phenolic, composite, and machined plastics components, delivering everything from single parts to fully assembled products built to print specifications. Its process capabilities include CAD/CAM design, CNC machining with nested-based production, drilling, finishing, profiling, sanding, shaping, mortise-and-tenon joinery, laminating, gluing, fingerjointing, paraffin treatment of lumber, and both commercial and Mil-Spec packaging. The facility offers standard, express, and urgent delivery options to meet varying lead-time requirements.

Valley Woodcraft serves customers in aerospace, aviation, defense, furniture, maritime, rail, transit, transportation, construction, and utilities. The company’s quality system is certified to ISO 9001 and AS 9100 for the manufacture of high-precision machined parts used in defense, aviation, aerospace, transportation, and other industries.

