, "ownership_tags": ["Veteran-owned", "Small business"]}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='valley-woodcraft-lumber-co' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Valley Woodworkers operates from Dunbar, West Virginia. The organization was founded in 2008 and functions as a woodworking club open to all skill levels. Its origins trace to a dual mission: training local residents in woodworking crafts and producing heirloom-quality wooden toys for the Salvation Army’s Christmas distribution to underprivileged children, a program ongoing since 1991.

The club holds monthly meetings on the second Thursday at its clubhouse on 12th Street, featuring project show-and-tell sessions and technical demonstrations. The facility serves as a gathering point rather than a commercial production shop; no headcount, square footage, or output volumes are published.

Participants range from beginners to professional woodworkers, while the toy program benefits children served by the Salvation Army. Local businesses such as Woodcraft and Withrow Supply in Huntington provide sponsorship and material support, including finishes, machinery, hardware, and sharpening services.

The group emphasizes community improvement through skill-sharing and charitable giving. Its distinguishing feature is the long-standing commitment to producing handcrafted toys for children in need, coupled with an open-door policy that welcomes anyone with an interest in woodworking.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Community service programs", "Woodworking demonstrations", "Toy production for charitable distribution", "Woodworking education workshops"], "industries": ["Community service"], "materials": [], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Monthly meetings with demonstrations and show-and-tell", "Heirloom toy production for Salvation Army since 1991", "Open membership regardless of skill level", "Supported by local suppliers Woodcraft and Withrow Supply"], "facts_used": ["Founded 2008 -> db", "Headquarters Dunbar, West Virginia -> db", "Monthly meetings on second Thursday -> /", "Clubhouse at 300 12th St, Dunbar, WV -> /", "Toy production for Salvation Army since 1991 -> db (description)", "Open membership to all skill levels -> /", "Sponsors: Woodcraft and Withrow Supply -> /", "Community service programs -> db (capabilities)"], "company_type": "Other", "makes_products": "no", "type_evidence": "The purpose of the Valley Woodworkers is to serve as a means for individuals interested in woodworking to meet fellow woodworkers and to share experiences, information, and ideas.", "founded_year": "2008", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='valley-woodworkers' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Valley Woodworks LLC is a custom furniture maker based in Palmer, Massachusetts. Founded in 2022 by Jonathan Dias, a Springfield College graduate with a background in business administration and entrepreneurial studies, the company began from his desire to create high-quality, handcrafted pieces that avoid the disposable nature of mass-produced furniture.

The shop produces custom tables and furniture using solid hardwood slabs selected for grain, moisture content, and character. No veneers, plywood cores, or shortcuts are used; each piece is finished with hand-rubbed hardwax oils that protect the wood while keeping its pores open and grain visible. Operations are carried out on a made-to-order basis, with no stated facility size or employee count beyond the founder.

Valley Woodworks serves residential clients seeking heirloom-quality dining tables, desks, and other furniture pieces. The company does not list specific commercial or industry clients, focusing instead on individual commissions that start with a design consultation.

Dias started the business to counter the click-to-buy culture and preserve the art of fine furniture making. The company emphasizes that its pieces are built to be passed down rather than replaced, a philosophy reflected in the choice of solid materials and traditional finishing methods.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Custom furniture manufacturing", "Solid hardwood slab selection", "Hand-rubbed hardwax oil finishing"], "industries": ["Custom furniture", "Residential furniture"], "materials": ["Solid hardwood"], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Solid hardwood slabs only \u2013 no veneers or plywood cores", "Hand-rubbed hardwax oil finishes that keep grain visible", "Custom-designed tables and furniture made to order", "Founded to preserve fine furniture craftsmanship against mass production"], "facts_used": ["Founded in 2022 by Jonathan Dias -> /about", "Located in Palmer, Massachusetts -> db", "Produces custom tables and furniture from solid hardwood slabs -> /", "Uses hand-rubbed hardwax oil finishes -> /", "No veneers or plywood cores -> /", "Founded to counter mass-produced furniture culture -> /about", "Jonathan Dias holds degree from Springfield College -> /about"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "Every Valley Woodworks piece begins as a solid hardwood slab, hand-selected for grain, moisture content, and character.", "founded_year": "2022", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='valley-woodworks-llc' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Vault Furniture operates from Caldwell, Idaho, where it was co-founded by designer Brandi. The company began as a maker of reclaimed-wood furniture and has grown into a high-end manufacturer of handcrafted shelving, desks, tables, and home accessories.

The shop produces made-to-order pieces using reclaimed old-growth pine, sustainably sourced ash and black walnut, American steel, and low-VOC finishes that carry GREENGUARD certification. Processes include custom design consultation, woodworking, metal fabrication, and finishing. All items are built in the Caldwell facility; home accessories and brackets typically ship in one to two weeks, while furniture and shelving units require three to four weeks.

Its product line spans wall-mounted shelving units, desks with integrated power, coffee and console tables, benches, bar carts, vases, wine racks, and pet feeders.

The business was founded on a pledge to create heirloom-quality furniture from sustainably sourced materials while providing exceptional customer service. Differentiators include free custom design support with co-founder Brandi, free shipping and exchanges within the contiguous United States, and a commitment to 100 percent U.S. handcrafting.', certifications=ARRAY['GREENGUARD Certified']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Custom furniture design", "Handcrafted woodworking", "Metal fabrication", "Low-VOC finishing", "Wall-mounted shelving production", "Made-to-order manufacturing", "Custom shelving design", "Free design consultation", "Shipping and returns management"], "industries": ["Furniture manufacturing", "Home decor", "Interior design"], "materials": ["Reclaimed old-growth pine", "Ash", "Black walnut", "American steel", "Low-VOC finishes (GREENGUARD certified)", "Brass"], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "1-2 weeks for accessories and brackets; 3-4 weeks for furniture and shelving units", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["100% handcrafted in Caldwell, Idaho", "Sustainably sourced solid wood, American steel, and GREENGUARD certified low-VOC finishes", "Free custom design consultation with co-founder Brandi", "Free shipping and exchanges in the contiguous U.S.", "Made-to-order production with 1\u20134 week lead times"], "facts_used": ["Location: Caldwell, Idaho -> /", "Co-founder: Brandi -> /", "Materials: reclaimed old-growth pine, ash, black walnut, American steel, low-VOC finishes -> /", "Certification: GREENGUARD certified finishes -> /", "Lead times: 1-2 weeks accessories, 3-4 weeks furniture -> /", "Free custom design consultation -> /", "Free shipping in contiguous US -> /", "Product categories: shelving, desks, tables, benches, carts, home decor -> /", "Company type: manufacturer -> /", "Mission: heirloom-quality furniture from sustainable materials -> /"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "A HIGH-END FURNITURE MANUFACTURER Vault furniture is proud to source sustainable materials for our handcrafted furniture and accessories. Additionally, our handmade furniture company manufactures products in the U.S. at our Caldwell, Idaho facility.", "founded_year": "", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='vault-furniture' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Vehicle Parts, operating as HQ 911, was founded in 1973 in Jefferson, Louisiana, as a family-run business serving the New Orleans metropolitan area. The company began as an installer of emergency vehicle equipment for local public safety agencies.

The shop designs, sells, and installs lighting, push bumpers, and other upfitting components for police, fire, and EMS vehicles. It carries more than 25 brands of parts, ranging from light bars to batteries, and provides repair services for existing installations. The facility on Deckbar Avenue in New Orleans handles both new vehicle builds and retrofit work.

Customers include municipal police departments, fire districts, and emergency medical service providers throughout the region. The company outfits patrol cars, fire apparatus, and ambulances with warning lights, sirens, consoles, and power management systems.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Emergency vehicle equipment installation", "Lighting installation", "Vehicle upfitting", "Equipment repair", "Parts distribution"], "industries": ["Police", "Fire", "EMS", "Emergency vehicles"], "materials": [], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Family-owned operation since 1973", "Stocks 25+ brands of emergency vehicle parts", "Specializes in lighting and electrical upfitting for police, fire, and EMS fleets", "Provides design, installation, and repair services in-house"], "facts_used": ["Founded in 1973 -> db", "Headquarters in Jefferson, Louisiana -> db", "Family-run business -> page /", "Designs, sells, and installs Police, Fire, EMS equipment -> page /", "Specializes in lighting and installations for emergency vehicles -> page /", "Stocks more than 25 brands of vehicle products -> page /", "Services: repairs, install, parts -> page /", "Serves police, fire, EMS customers -> page /"], "company_type": "Installer / service company", "makes_products": "no", "type_evidence": "Founded in 1973, Vehicle Parts/HQ 911 is the premier emergency equipment installer in the New Orleans area.", "founded_year": "1973", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": ["Family-owned"]}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='vehicle-parts' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Velmar Food Services operates from Phoenix, Arizona, where Richard and Judith Barton founded the family-owned company in 1974. The business traces its recipes to Richard''s father, who applied his culinary craftsmanship to develop the perfect burrito. Now a third-generation family-run enterprise, Velmar has grown from supplying mobile food services to serving unified school districts across Arizona and California.

The company manufactures its Arizona Gold brand of Mexican cuisine — including burritos, appetizers, entrees, side dishes, and desserts — using locally produced tortillas, robust beans, cheese, green chiles, fresh eggs, and choice meats. In addition to production, Velmar runs a foodservice distribution operation that stocks breakfast, lunch, center-of-the-plate entrees, and desserts from top labels. Its warehouse and freezer facilities also provide pallet storage leasing for other food businesses needing seasonal or overflow capacity.

Velmar''s customers include restaurants, delis, convenience stores, healthcare facilities, correctional operations, and school districts throughout Arizona and California. The Arizona Gold line has become a staple in school meal programs, while the distribution side supplies a broad range of foodservice operators through local distributors.

Velmar emphasizes cultural authenticity and flavor maximization while minimizing cost, a philosophy rooted in the founding family''s recipes. The company differentiates itself by combining manufacturing, distribution, and warehousing under one roof, allowing customers to simplify procurement from a single source. Community involvement, including sponsorship of local charities, is also cited as a core value.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Food manufacturing (Mexican cuisine)", "Foodservice distribution", "Warehousing and cold storage leasing", "Product development and recipe innovation", "Culinary recipe development", "Private label manufacturing (Arizona Gold brand)"], "industries": ["Restaurants", "Delis", "Convenience stores", "Healthcare facilities", "Correctional facilities", "School districts (K-12)", "Foodservice operators"], "materials": ["Spices", "Tortillas", "Beans", "Cheese", "Green chiles", "Eggs", "Beef", "Poultry", "Seafood"], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Third-generation family ownership with recipes dating to founding", "Arizona-locally grown and manufactured products", "Integrated manufacturing, distribution, and warehousing services", "Warehouse and freezer space available for lease", "Active community sponsorship and charitable giving"], "facts_used": ["Founded 1974 by Richard and Judith Barton -> about-us", "Family-owned, third-generation -> home, about-us", "Arizona Gold brand manufactured products -> home, about-us", "Product categories: appetizers, entrees, side dishes, desserts -> home", "Distribution to restaurants, delis, convenience stores, healthcare, corrections, school districts -> home", "Warehouse and freezer space for lease -> home, about-us", "Ingredients: tortillas, beans, cheese, green chiles, eggs, meats -> about-us", "Community sponsorship of local charities -> about-us", "Headquarters Phoenix, AZ -> home"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_p