UPDATE companies SET description='Velocity Metalworks was founded in 1970 and operates from two Illinois locations: its headquarters in Hoffman and a second facility in Belleville.

The shop delivers full-service metal manufacturing, encompassing tool and die building, precision metal stamping, fabrication, CNC machining, EDM, assembly, and finishing services such as powder coating and polishing. It positions itself as a total supply-chain partner, handling engineering, design, prototyping, production, and fulfillment under one roof. Facility sizes and headcount are not disclosed.

Velocity serves tier‑1 suppliers and OEMs across demanding industries, though specific sectors are not named on its website.

The company’s stated mission is to manufacture metal solutions so customers who value “Made in America” can compete and win. It differentiates itself through a multi‑layered quality system — continuous in‑process inspections, a double‑check setup verification, and a culture of shared quality ownership — backed by ISO 9001:2015 certification.', certifications=ARRAY['ISO 9001:2015']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Tool & die building", "Metal stamping", "Metal fabrication", "CNC machining", "EDM (Electrical Discharge Machining)", "Assembly", "Powder coating", "Wet painting", "Polishing", "Engineering & design", "Prototyping", "Fulfillment & logistics", "Contract manufacturing"], "industries": ["Tier 1 manufacturers", "OEM manufacturers"], "materials": [], "equipment": ["CNC machines", "EDM machines"], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Full-service supply chain partner from design through delivery (engineering, prototyping, manufacturing, assembly, fulfillment)", "ISO 9001:2015 certified quality management system", "Multi-layered quality process with continuous inspections and double-check verification", "Over 50 years of experience in tool & die, stamping, and fabrication", "Lean, low-overhead operation focused on cost savings and value"], "facts_used": ["Founded 1970 -> db", "Headquarters in Hoffman, IL and second facility in Belleville, IL -> /", "Provides full-service tool & die, metal stamping, fabrication, contract manufacturing -> /", "Serves tier 1 & OEM manufacturers -> /", "ISO 9001:2015 certified -> /quality", "Quality system: continuous inspections, double-check, program packets -> /quality", "Mission: manufacture metal solutions for Made in America customers -> /about", "Offers engineering, design, prototyping, assembly, fulfillment -> /about", "Finishing: powder coating, painting, polishing -> /", "CNC and EDM capabilities -> db description"], "company_type": "Contract manufacturer / job shop", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "Velocity Metalworks provides full-service tool & die, metal stamping, fabrication and contract manufacturing for tier 1 & OEM manufacturers", "founded_year": "1970", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": ["https://www.linkedin.com/company/velocity-metalworks2/"], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='velocity-metalworks' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Vergent Products operates from Loveland, Colorado, where it was founded in 1996. The company was established on two core principles: exceptional client experience and the engagement of a diverse team of experts focused on continually elevating client success.

The firm provides end-to-end electronics design and manufacturing, spanning product design (electrical, mechanical, firmware/software), printed circuit board assembly on multiple SMT lines with robotic selective solder and hand solder, 100% automated optical inspection, X-ray inspection, functional and in-circuit testing, final product assembly, system integration, configure-to-order, warranty and repair services, and supply chain management including 3PL distribution, advanced component stocking, and risk mitigation. Its quality system integrates ERP, PDM, and MES in a fully digital factory with full traceability and a proprietary preventive system. Facility size and headcount are not disclosed.

The company emphasizes unsurpassed on-time delivery, a 100% digital factory with integrated ERP/PDM/MES, full traceability, and a proprietary preventive system as key differentiators. It was started to deliver a complete and comprehensive product delivery experience, promising kept commitments, mutual trust, and uncommon dedication to the client’s mission.', certifications=ARRAY['ISO 9001:2015','AS9100D','ISO 13485:2016']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Product design (electrical, mechanical, firmware/software)", "PCB assembly (SMT, selective solder, hand solder)", "Automated optical inspection (AOI)", "X-ray inspection", "Functional testing", "In-circuit testing (ICT)", "Final product assembly", "System integration", "Configure to order", "Warranty and repair services", "Order fulfillment and 3PL distribution", "Component sourcing support", "Advanced component stocking", "Supply chain risk management", "Rapid prototyping", "Sustaining engineering", "High voltage test development", "Test engineering development", "Program management", "Structured new product introduction (NPI) process", "Measurement and controls manufacturing", "Part kitting", "3PL shipping", "Repair and return processing"], "industries": ["Medical devices", "Measurement and controls", "Aerospace and defense", "Industrial and critical environment", "Energy generation and alternative energy", "Automotive electrical systems"], "materials": [], "equipment": ["Multiple SMT lines", "Robotic selective solder", "Hand solder stations", "Automated optical inspection (AOI) systems", "X-ray inspection systems", "In-circuit test (ICT) equipment", "Functional test equipment"], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Unsurpassed on-time delivery", "100% digital factory with integrated ERP, PDM, and MES", "Full traceability and proprietary preventive quality system", "Advanced component stocking and supply chain risk mitigation", "Multiple SMT lines with 100% AOI and X-ray inspection"], "facts_used": ["Founded in 1996 -> db", "Headquarters Loveland, Colorado -> db", "Certifications ISO 9001:2015, AS9100D, ISO 13485:2016 -> /", "Capabilities: PCBA, assembly, test, design, supply chain -> /capabilities", "Industries: Medical, Measurement & Controls, Aerospace & Defense, Industrial & Critical Environment -> /", "Industries: Energy generation, alternative energy, Automotive electrical systems -> db", "Differentiators: Unsurpassed On-Time Delivery, Integrated ERP/PDM/MES, 100% Digital Factory, Full Traceability, Proprietary Preventive System -> /capabilities", "Founding principles: exceptional client experience, diverse team engagement -> /about-us", "Complete product delivery company -> /about-us", "Equipment: Multiple SMT lines, robotic selective solder, AOI, X-ray, ICT -> /capabilities"], "company_type": "Contract manufacturer / job shop", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "Contract Manufacturing PCBA Box Build Program & Test Product Design", "founded_year": "1996", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='vergent-products' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Vermillion Inc. was established in 1965 in Wichita, Kansas. The company operates a 43,000-square-foot manufacturing facility in the city.

Vermillion specializes in custom cable solutions, including bulk cable production, custom-designed cable assemblies, and molded assemblies. The facility produces cables with conductor ranges from 0 to 28 AWG using materials such as tinned, nickel-plated, and silver-plated copper. Shielding options include the proprietary Vermalloy® alloys, Aracon® aramid fibers, and various foil and Mylar configurations. Jacketing materials span high-temperature ETFE, PTFE, PFA, low-smoke zero-halogen polyethylene, and braided or blown-on jackets made from Nomex, Kevlar, PEEK, Viton®, and other polymers. The company emphasizes engineering consultation and serves as a resource for prototype and initial production runs.

The primary markets are military and aerospace. Vermillion has been recognized by Rockwell Collins as Wire and Cable Supplier of the Year multiple times, most recently noted in 2009. Its products meet stringent defense and aviation standards, supported by certifications to ISO 9001 and AS9100.

Vermillion differentiates itself through its proprietary Vermalloy® shielding material, described as the most effective secure-voice shielding available, and through in-house certified trainers for J-STD-001 soldering specifications.', certifications=ARRAY['ISO 9001:2008','AS9100C','J-STD-001']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Bulk cable production", "Custom cable design and engineering", "Molded cable assemblies", "Cable shielding (Vermalloy\u00ae, tinned copper, nickel-plated copper, silver-plated copper, Aracon\u00ae, foil/Mylar shields)", "Cable jacketing (ETFE, PTFE, PFA, LSZH polyethylene, braided jackets: polyester, Nomex, Kevlar, PEEK, Teflon-impregnated fiberglass, fiberglass; blown-on jackets: neoprene, EPDM, Viton\u00ae)", "Engineering and design consultation", "J-STD-001 soldering", "Electrical testing (DIT-MCO 2500/2650)", "Prototype and initial production runs"], "industries": ["Military", "Aerospace"], "materials": ["Tinned Copper", "Nickel Plated Copper", "Silver Plated Copper", "Vermalloy\u00ae 622", "Vermalloy\u00ae 3948", "Flattened Tinned Copper", "Aracon\u00ae Aramid Fibers", "Copper Foil (with and without drain wire)", "Aluminum Foil (with and without drain wire)", "Copper Mylar (with and without drain wire)", "Aluminum Mylar (with and without drain wire)", "150\u00b0 ETFE", "200\u00b0 ETFE", "Polyethylene (Low Smoke Zero Halogen)", "PTFE", "PFA", "Polyester", "Nomex", "Kevlar", "PEEK", "Teflon Impregnated Fiberglass", "Fiberglass", "Neoprene", "EPDM", "Viton\u00ae"], "equipment": ["DIT-MCO 2500", "DIT-MCO 2650.MTA"], "volume": "Prototype and initial production orders", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Proprietary Vermalloy\u00ae shielding for secure voice applications", "ISO 9001 certified since 1996; AS9100 certified since 2003", "J-STD-001 certified soldering with in-house trainers", "43,000 sq. ft. manufacturing facility in Wichita, KS", "Custom cable design from prototype through initial production"], "facts_used": ["Founded 1965 -> db, /", "Headquarters Wichita, Kansas -> db, /", "43,000 sq. ft. manufacturing facility -> /", "ISO 9001 certified since 1996 -> /, /quality", "AS9100 certified since 2003 -> /quality", "J-STD-001 certified soldering with in-house trainers -> /quality", "Kansas Award for Excellence 1996-1998 -> /, /quality", "Military and aerospace industries -> /", "Rockwell Collins Wire and Cable Supplier of the Year (2009) -> /quality", "Vermalloy\u00ae proprietary shielding material -> /, /capabilities", "Conductor range 0-28 AWG -> /capabilities", "Conductor materials: tinned copper, nickel plated copper, silver plated copper -> /capabilities", "Shielding materials: Vermalloy\u00ae 622, 3948, tinned copper, flattened tinned copper, nickel plated copper, silver plated copper, Aracon\u00ae, copper foil, aluminum foil, copper mylar, aluminum mylar -> /capabilities", "Jacketing materials: 150\u00b0 ETFE, 200\u00b0 ETFE, LSZH polyethylene, PTFE, PFA, braided jackets (polyester, Nomex, Kevlar, PEEK, Teflon impregnated fiberglass, fiberglass), blown-on jackets (neoprene, EPDM, Viton\u00ae) -> /capabilities", "Testing equipment DIT-MCO 2500 and 2650.MTA -> /quality", "Custom cable design capability, prototypes and initial production orders -> /, /capabilities", "Molded assemblies -> /"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "Modern, 43,000 sq. ft. manufacturing facility", "founded_year": "1965", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='vermillion-inc' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Vermont Electric Power Company (VELCO) is headquartered in Rutland, Vermont. The company was created in 1956 as the nation’s first statewide, transmission-only utility, formed to build and operate an interconnected high-voltage grid that would deliver and share access to clean power, including hydroelectric resources, across Vermont. Ownership is structured uniquely: the company is held by the state’s 17 distribution utilities and a public benefits corporation, with a for-profit model designed to return value to those owners, their customers, and all Vermonters.

VELCO owns and operates Vermont’s high-voltage transmission system, delivering bulk electricity to local distribution utilities rather than directly to homes or businesses. Its core activities include grid operation, maintenance, and planning to ensure a reliable, affordable, safe, secure, and sustainable transmission network. The company also provides a unified voice on regional energy issues. While specific facility sizes and headcount are not disclosed, VELCO serves the 17 member distribution utilities that collectively supply power throughout the state.

The primary customers are those 17 distribution utilities, which include municipal departments such as Barton Village Electric Department, Burlington Electric Department, Hardwick Electric Department, and others listed in the company’s public materials. Indirectly, VELCO’s transmission services support every electricity consumer in Vermont. The company operates within the electric power transmission and clean energy sectors, with a stated focus on environmental stewardship and sustainability.

VELCO differentiates itself through its pioneering transmission-only structure, its ownership model that aligns incentives with public benefit, and its mission to serve as a partner. The company emphasizes safety as a core value, publishes an annual ESG report, and promotes a culture of belonging and innovation to advance a sustainable energy future for Vermont.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Electric transmission grid operation", "High-voltage transmission system management", "Clean power delivery (hydroelectric)", "Grid reliability and security management", "Regional energy advocacy and coordination", "Transmission planning and maintenance", "Environmental stewardship and sustainability programs", "Workforce safety and belonging initiatives"], "industries": ["Electric power transmission", "Clean energy", "Public utilities"], "materials": [], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Nation''s first statewide transmission-only company", "Owned by 17 distribution utilities and a public benefits corporation", "For-profit structure returning value to owners, customers, and Vermonters", "Focus on reliable, affordable, safe, secure, and sustainable high-voltage grid", "Unified voice on regional energy issues"], "facts_used": ["Headquarters: Rutland, Vermont -> db", "Founded: 1956 -> /about", "Ownership: 17 distribution utilities and a public benefits corporation -> /about", "Mission: serve as a trusted partner -> /about", "Vision: create a sustainable Vermont -> /about", "Transmission-only company, first statewide -> /about", "Delivers clean power including hydro -> /about", "Member utilities listed (e.g., Barton Village, Burlington Electric) -> db", "Focus on reliability, affordability, safety, security, sustainability -> /about", "2024 ESG Report published -> /about", "Safety as core value -> /about", "People & Belonging initiative -> /about"], "company_type": "Installer / service company", "makes_pr