UPDATE companies SET description='VoltServer is headquartered in East Greenwich, Rhode Island. The company was founded by Stephen Eaves, who serves as CEO, and has a 10-year deployment history as of 2024. Matt Giuliano holds the role of EVP and GM, Emeritus, Communications and In-Building.

VoltServer develops and manufactures Digital Electricity™ (DE), a patented fault-managed power system classified as Class 4 under the 2023 National Electrical Code. The technology splits energy into packets transferred from a Transmitter unit to a Receiver unit, with safety monitoring after each packet. The company reports more than 1,000 building installations and 40,000 circuits across large venues.

The company serves telecommunications service providers deploying 5G and Wi-Fi networks, transportation hubs such as ports and airports, enterprise buildings and campuses, industrial manufacturing facilities, data centers, and building electrification projects. VoltServer also collaborates with partners including Cisco, where it holds Select Developer status for IIoT power solutions, and Eaton for critical infrastructure.

VoltServer states its technology reduces installation time by using existing data pathways and hybrid fiber cable, lowers material costs by eliminating conduit, and improves safety by halting hazardous current within milliseconds. The platform is designed for energy efficiency and can qualify for LEED credits. The company says it is driven by innovation and aims to set the standard in fault-managed power systems.', certifications=ARRAY['NEC 2023 (National Electrical Code) - Fault-Managed Power Systems / Class 4 Power','Underwriters Laboratory (UL) - Fault-Managed Power Systems / Class 4 Power']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Digital Electricity\u2122 system design and deployment", "Fault-managed power system integration", "Remote power solutions for distributed networks", "Transmitter unit manufacturing", "Receiver unit manufacturing", "Real-time device telemetry and dashboard monitoring", "Remote software updates without power interruption", "Policy control for automated actions", "Class 2 wiring methods for high-power device energization", "Hybrid fiber cable integration", "End-to-end power distribution system engineering"], "industries": ["Telecommunications", "Transportation", "Enterprise Buildings and Campuses", "Industrial Manufacturing", "Data Centers", "Building Electrification"], "materials": [], "equipment": ["Transmitter unit", "Receiver unit", "Hybrid fiber cable"], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Patented Digital Electricity\u2122 packet energy transfer technology", "Class 4 fault-managed power recognized in 2023 NEC and UL standards", "Power delivery over existing data pathways and hybrid fiber cable", "Inherent safety: fault detection and current halt within milliseconds", "Cisco Select Developer partner for IIoT power solutions"], "facts_used": ["Headquarters: East Greenwich, Rhode Island -> db", "Founder: Stephen Eaves, CEO and Founder -> /about", "Executive: Matt Giuliano, EVP and GM -> /", "Technology: Digital Electricity\u2122, fault-managed power, Class 4 -> /about, /", "Patented packet energy transfer -> /about", "Transmitter and Receiver units -> /about", "Scale: 1,000+ building installations, 40,000+ circuits -> /about", "Industries served: Service Provider, Transportation Networks, Enterprise Buildings and Campuses, Industrial Manufacturing, Data Centers, Building Electrification -> /about, /", "Partnerships: Cisco Select Developer, Eaton -> /", "Certifications: NEC 2023, UL for Fault-Managed Power Systems/Class 4 Power -> /about", "LEED credit qualification -> /about", "Safety: fault detection in milliseconds -> /about", "Deployment: existing data pathways, hybrid fiber cable -> /about", "Cost effective: reduces conduit, material costs -> /about", "Energy efficient -> /about", "Real-time telemetry, dashboard, remote updates, policy control -> /about"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "VoltServer''s leading-edge Digital Electricity technologies have provided optimal, efficient, and resilient power solutions around the world for more than a decade.", "founded_year": "", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": ["https://www.linkedin.com/company/voltserver/"], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='voltserver' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='W. L. Gore & Associates, Inc. operates its Paper Mill West facility in Newark, Delaware. The company was founded in 1958 by Bill and Vieve Gore in their family home, and has grown into a global materials science enterprise with approximately 13,000 associates across five continents.

Gore develops and manufactures a broad portfolio of high-performance materials and products, including cables and assemblies, fabrics, fibers and thread, filtration and purification media, gaskets and sealants, medical devices, pharmaceutical bioprocessing components, proton exchange membranes for clean energy, thermal insulation, and protective vents. The company’s materials science expertise underpins thousands of product variations produced at facilities worldwide.

Its customers span aerospace and defense, apparel and textiles, automotive and electrified vehicles, chemicals, electronics, energy, fire and public safety, industrial manufacturing, life sciences, semiconductors, telecommunications, and test and measurement. Concrete applications include microwave RF test cables for aerospace and semiconductor test equipment, GORE-TEX fabrics for consumer and professional outerwear, implantable medical devices, and filter bags that capture 99.99% of emissions in industrial plants.

The company attributes its differentiation to a culture of innovation rooted in materials science, citing 65 years of continuous R&D, rigorous testing and analysis for every material, and proprietary technologies such as ultra-low degradation proton exchange membranes for hydrogen production and high-speed data cables up to 60% lighter than industry standards.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Cable assembly", "Fabric manufacturing", "Fiber and thread production", "Filtration media manufacturing", "Gasket and sealant manufacturing", "Medical device manufacturing", "Pharmaceutical bioprocessing component manufacturing", "Proton exchange membrane manufacturing", "Thermal insulation manufacturing", "Vent manufacturing", "Microwave RF test cable assembly", "High-speed data cable assembly", "Filter bag production", "Materials testing and analysis"], "industries": ["Aerospace & Defense", "Apparel & Textiles", "Automotive / Electrified Vehicles", "Chemicals", "Electronics", "Energy", "Fire & Public Safety/Police", "Industrial & Manufacturing", "Life Sciences", "Semiconductor", "Telecommunications", "Test & Measurement"], "materials": [], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": [], "facts_used": ["Founded in 1958 by Bill and Vieve Gore in their family home -> /about", "Approximately 13,000 associates globally -> db", "Headquartered in Newark, Delaware -> db", "Product categories: cables & assemblies, fabrics, fibers & thread, filtration & purification, gaskets & sealants, medical, PharmBIO, PEM technology, thermal insulation, vents -> /", "Industries served: aerospace & defense, apparel & textiles, automotive/electrified vehicles, chemicals, electronics, energy, fire & public safety, industrial manufacturing, life sciences, semiconductor, telecommunications, test & measurement -> /", "65 years of innovation -> /about", "Ultra-low degradation PEM for hydrogen production -> /", "High-speed data cables up to 60% lighter -> /", "Filter bags with 99.99% emissions capture -> /"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "Gore is a global materials science company with approximately 13,000 Associates spanning five continents and thousands of products across industries", "founded_year": "1958", "employee_count": "13,000", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='w-l-gore-associates-inc-paper-mill-west' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='The Bowers Group operates its sheet metal division from Beltsville, Maryland, with a second fabrication facility in Virginia. The company was established in 1984 and has served the mechanical construction, service, and repair market across Maryland, Virginia, and Washington, D.C. for over three decades. It functions as a Legence company (Nasdaq: LGN), a publicly traded provider of engineering, consulting, installation, and maintenance services for mission-critical building systems.

The in-house sheet metal department fabricates and installs more than 8 million pounds of sheet metal annually. ft. in Maryland and 30,000 sq. ft. in Virginia — dedicated to sheet metal fabrication and sub-assembly. The shops run Vicon coil lines, coil-fed plasma tables, and water jet insulation cutters, supported by BIM-based CADD coordination. Additional capabilities include specialty piping prefab, steel piping prefab, and full quality control and commissioning programs that span preconstruction through project closeout.

Clients include general contractors, high-technology firms, hospitals and institutional facilities, government agencies, and property management companies. The company focuses on commercial and mission-critical projects, delivering HVAC, process piping, and other mechanical, electrical, and plumbing (MEP) systems for new construction and retrofit work throughout the Mid-Atlantic region.

The Bowers Group states its mission is to provide solutions rather than just products, emphasizing superior service, cost efficiency, and reliability. Its quality control division assigns personnel to each project at the start of construction to verify that work meets design specifications and customer requirements, aiming to identify and resolve potential delays before they affect the schedule.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Sheet metal fabrication", "Sheet metal installation", "CADD / BIM coordination", "Quality control and commissioning", "Specialty piping prefabrication", "Steel piping prefabrication", "Commercial mechanical service", "Mission critical retrofit and service", "Service construction", "Sub-assembly", "Coil line fabrication", "Plasma cutting", "Water jet insulation cutting"], "industries": ["General contractors", "High-technology firms", "Hospitals and institutional facilities", "Government agencies", "Property management", "Commercial construction", "Mission critical facilities", "Mechanical construction"], "materials": [], "equipment": ["Vicon coil lines", "Coil-fed plasma tables", "Water jet insulation cutters", "BIM software"], "volume": "Over 8 million lbs of sheet metal annually", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["8 million lbs annual sheet metal fabrication capacity", "In-house BIM coordination with Vicon coil lines and coil-fed plasma tables", "Quality control program from preconstruction through project closeout", "24/7 support for service and retrofit work"], "facts_used": ["Founded 1984 -> /about-us", "Headquarters Beltsville, MD -> / (home page) and /about-us", "Legence company (Nasdaq: LGN) -> /about-us", "8 million lbs annual sheet metal capacity -> / (home page)", "60,000 sq ft Maryland + 30,000 sq ft Virginia fabrication space -> / (home page)", "Vicon coil lines, coil-fed plasma tables, water jet insulation cutters -> / (home page)", "BIM/CADD coordination -> /services and / (home page)", "Quality control program preconstruction through closeout -> /quality", "Clients: general contractors, high-tech firms, hospitals, government agencies, property management -> /about-us", "Service area: Maryland, Virginia, Washington D.C. -> /about-us", "Services: sheet metal, specialty piping prefab, steel piping prefab, commercial service, mission critical retrofit -> /services and db", "Mission: provide solutions instead of products, superior service -> /about-us and db"], "company_type": "Contract manufacturer / job shop", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "The Bowers Group in-house sheet metal department has capabilities to fabricate and install over 8 million lbs of sheet metal annually.", "founded_year": "1984", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='w-e-bowers-sheet-metal-shop' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='WC Woodworks, Hardwoods, & Sawmill operates from Ocala, Florida, where it has been a family-owned business since 1987. The company traces its roots to 1973 when Robert Ross, then 18, began collecting tools and developing a passion for woodworking. What started as a hobby evolved into a commercial venture in 1987, with Robert, his wife Robin, and their sons Ryan and Russell running the operation.

The firm supplies specialty hardwood lumber, maintaining an inventory of more than 40 domestic and tropical exotic species that it describes as the largest in North Central Florida. An on-site sawmill and production facility enable custom milling, dimensioning, and fabrication services. The shop also builds custom furniture and cabinetry, and offers furniture repair.

Customers include professional woodworkers and hobbyist craftsmen seeking premium hardwoods, millwork, and custom wood products. The company serves both trade buyers who need specific dimensions and individuals selecting boards in person at the lumber racks.

