UPDATE companies SET description='Westinghouse Electric Co LLC is headquartered in Hopkins, South Carolina. The company traces its origins to 1869 when George Westinghouse founded Westinghouse Electric, beginning a legacy of engineering innovation that later extended into nuclear energy.

Today Westinghouse designs and supplies nuclear reactor technology, fuel, and services for the global nuclear fleet. The company reports approximately 12,500 employees across more than 100 locations in 23 countries, and supplies over 100,000 nuclear parts annually.

Its technology underpins 57 percent of the world''s operating nuclear reactors, and the company maintains nearly two-thirds of the global fleet while fueling 40 percent of it. Recent projects include conditional purchase orders with Polish suppliers for the first AP1000 unit at Lubiatowo-Kopalino, full clevis bolt replacement at Sweden''s Ringhals plant, and delivery of the final ITER vacuum vessel sector.

The company''s founding principle—making technology better, faster, and more efficient—remains its differentiator. Westinghouse supplied the world''s first commercial pressurized water reactor in 1957, and its technology remains the basis for roughly half of today''s operating reactors. It positions itself as an indispensable partner for scaling nuclear energy to meet rising global demand.', certifications=ARRAY['ASME']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Nuclear reactor design and engineering", "Nuclear plant maintenance and outage services", "Nuclear fuel supply and engineering", "Integrated learning management system (LMS) services", "User support services", "Nuclear parts manufacturing and supply", "AP1000 Generation III+ reactor deployment", "Advanced Donut Bolt Technology installation", "bertha\u2122 AI knowledge assistant for nuclear industry"], "industries": ["Nuclear energy", "Electric power generation", "Nuclear technology services", "Fusion research"], "materials": [], "equipment": ["AP1000 pressurized water reactor", "APX Fleet", "bertha\u2122 Technology", "Advanced Donut Bolt Technology"], "volume": "Over 100,000 nuclear parts annually", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["World''s first commercial pressurized water reactor (1957)", "Technology powers 57% of world''s nuclear power plants", "Maintains nearly two-thirds of world''s nuclear fleet", "Fuels 40% of world''s nuclear fleet", "Approx. 12,500 employees across 100+ locations in 23 countries"], "facts_used": ["Headquartered in Hopkins, South Carolina -> db", "Founded in 1869 by George Westinghouse -> db, /about-us", "Approximately 12,500 employees -> /about-us", "100+ locations in 23 countries -> /about-us", "Supplies over 100,000 nuclear parts annually -> db (products)", "Technology powers 57% of world''s nuclear power plants -> /", "Maintains nearly two-thirds of world''s nuclear fleet -> /", "Fuels 40% of world''s nuclear fleet -> /", "World''s first commercial pressurized water re