UPDATE companies SET description='Wire Machine Systems was founded in 1987 in Fort Wayne, Indiana. The company entered the market as a supplier of equipment and services to the wire, cable, bar, and tube industries, positioning itself as a one-stop shop for machinery, spare parts, and technical support.

The firm provides state-of-the-art manufacturing equipment — including drawbenches, roll pointers, shot blasting systems, buncher bows, wire straighteners, and spring coiling machines — along with spare parts for European and Asian machinery. A centralized warehouse in Fort Wayne stocks replacement components for a wide range of equipment, allowing the company to ship parts quickly even for machines it did not originally supply.

